          "stage": "strategize",
          "report": "{\n  \"computed_at\": \"2026-05-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"lookback_scans\": 5,\n  \"focus_dimensions\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Error consistency\",\n      \"reason\": \"Declining trend (88.5 -> 86.0), highest headroom at 14.0, and massive rework loop (113 resolved, 8 reopened). This dimension is actively regressing and has the most churn of any subjective dimension.\",\n      \"headroom\": 14.0,\n      \"trend\": \"declining\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Low elegance\",\n      \"reason\": \"Stagnant at 87.5 with 12.5 headroom and zero recent investment. High-weight dimension (w=12) that has been neglected for multiple cycles.\",\n      \"headroom\": 12.5,\n      \"trend\": \"stagnant\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Mid elegance\",\n      \"reason\": \"Improved from 82 to 87.5 but now stagnant for 3 scans. High-weight dimension (w=22) with 12.5 headroom. Recent investment of 1 cluster is insufficient for a dimension this weighted.\",\n      \"headroom\": 12.5,\n      \"trend\": \"improving\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Test health\",\n      \"reason\": \"Declining trend (94.5 -> 87.2) with verified_strict_score of only 58.6, indicating a large gap between reported and actual coverage. This is the biggest verified-vs-strict discrepancy in the entire scorecard.\",\n      \"headroom\": 12.8,\n      \"trend\": \"declining\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Duplication\",\n      \"reason\": \"Stagnant at 85.9 strict with 14.1 headroom, worst dimension gap per debt_trajectory. The boilerplate_duplication detector has 6/6 failing (0.3 pass rate) which is an outlier.\",\n      \"headroom\": 14.1,\n      \"trend\": \"stagnant\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"avoid_areas\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Abstraction fit\",\n      \"reason\": \"83 resolved issues with 6 reopens. The subjective reviewer keeps flagging single-impl interfaces, passthrough delegation, and options bags - all of which are intentional SOLID patterns per project rules. Further work here is pure churn.\",\n      \"type\": \"rework-loop\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Cross-module arch\",\n      \"reason\": \"71 resolved with 0 reopens but score plateaued at 91.0 for 3 scans. Investment has diminishing returns; 2 remaining open issues are minor (dead re-export, self-referencing import).\",\n      \"type\": \"diminishing-returns\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Convention drift\",\n      \"reason\": \"59 resolved with only 1 open. Score improved from 87.5 to 90.5 and stabilized. The remaining open issue is minor (module-level helpers). No investment needed.\",\n      \"type\": \"diminishing-returns\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Auth consistency\",\n      \"reason\": \"Already at 95.0 with only 5.0 headroom. Low-weight dimension (w=1). Any work here is score-neutral.\",\n      \"type\": \"score-neutral\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Init coupling\",\n      \"reason\": \"Already at 96.0 with only 4.0 headroom. Low-weight dimension (w=1). No meaningful score improvement possible.\",\n      \"type\": \"score-neutral\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rework_warnings\": [\n    {\n      \"dimension\": \"error_consistency\",\n      \"resolved\": 113,\n      \"new_open\": 1,\n      \"files\": [\".\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dimension\": \"mid_level_elegance\",\n      \"resolved\": 78,\n      \"new_open\": 1,\n      \"files\": [\".\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dimension\": \"abstraction_fitness\",\n      \"resolved\": 83,\n      \"new_open\": 1,\n      \"files\": [\".\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dimension\": \"low_level_elegance\",\n      \"resolved\": 68,\n      \"new_open\": 2,\n      \"files\": [\".\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"file_churn_hotspots\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"src/cli/sync-command.ts\",\n      \"count\": 8,\n      \"detectors\": [\"props\", \"smells\", \"stale_wontfix\", \"structural\", \"subjective_review\", \"unused\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"src/cli/types.ts\",\n      \"count\": 7,\n      \"detectors\": [\"exports\", \"props\", \"test_coverage\", \"unused\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"src/vcs/authenticated-git-ops.ts\",\n      \"count\": 11,\n      \"detectors\": [\"boilerplate_duplication\", \"cycles\", \"exports\", \"responsibility_cohesion\", \"single_use\", \"subjective_review\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"src/settings/labels/processor.ts\",\n      \"count\": 8,\n      \"detectors\": [\"boilerplate_duplication\", \"smells\", \"subjective_review\", \"test_coverage\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"src/config/types.ts\",\n      \"count\": 16,\n      \"detectors\": [\"exports\", \"structural\", \"test_coverage\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"src/settings/rulesets/index.ts\",\n      \"count\": 24,\n      \"detectors\": [\"exports\", \"facade\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"stagnant_dimensions\": [\n    \"AI generated debt\",\n    \"Duplication\",\n    \"File health\",\n    \"High elegance\",\n    \"Low elegance\",\n    \"Security\"\n  ],\n  \"debt_trend\": \"stable\",\n  \"score_trend\": \"improving\",\n  \"momentum_dimensions\": [\n    \"Code quality\",\n    \"Contracts\",\n    \"Cross-module arch\",\n    \"Logic clarity\",\n    \"Mid elegance\",\n    \"Structure nav\",\n    \"Type safety\"\n  ],\n  \"executive_summary\": \"The codebase has reached 90.6 strict score (all-time high) with an improving trend, but momentum is stalling. Three consecutive scans at 90.6 suggest the easy gains are exhausted. The highest-leverage opportunities are now in neglected high-weight dimensions: Low elegance (w=12, stagnant at 87.5), Mid elegance (w=22, plateaued at 87.5), and Error consistency (w=3, actively declining to 86.0). Duplication is the worst strict dimension at 85.9 with a 0.3 pass rate on boilerplate_duplication, making it a clear target.\\n\\nThe execution pattern reveals a 46.4% skip rate (199 skipped vs 132 done) with 145 false-positive skips. This is healthy triaging, not avoidance - but the 205 wontfix count is concerning. The rework loops in error_consistency (8 reopens), mid_level_elegance (10 reopens), and abstraction_fitness (6 reopens) indicate the subjective reviewer keeps re-flagging resolved patterns. For abstraction_fitness specifically, this is driven by the reviewer not understanding SOLID DI patterns, and further investment there should be avoided.\\n\\nTest health shows the most alarming discrepancy: strict score 87.2 vs verified_strict_score 58.6. This 28.6-point gap suggests the test coverage detector is being overly generous, or coverage claims are not matching reality. This dimension also declined from 94.5 to 87.2 and has been flat for 4 scans. Addressing test health would have outsized impact on real codebase resilience even if it does not move the headline score much.\",\n  \"observe_guidance\": \"Focus verification effort on Error consistency (declining, high headroom), Low elegance (stagnant, neglected), and Duplication (worst strict score). Skip verification of Auth consistency, Init coupling, Security, and Stale migration - these are already strong with minimal headroom. Watch for the Test health verified-vs-strict gap; any test coverage findings should be scrutinized for accuracy. Do not waste cycles re-verifying Abstraction fit or Cross-module arch - these are plateau zones where the reviewer keeps re-flagging intentional SOLID patterns.\",\n  \"reflect_guidance\": \"The focus dimensions for this cycle should be Error consistency, Low elegance, Mid elegance, and Duplication - all have double-digit headroom and are either declining or stagnant. Avoid Abstraction fit (rework trap from SOLID false positives), Cross-module arch (diminishing returns at 91.0), and all dimensions already above 95.0. The recurring rework loops in error_consistency and mid_level_elegance suggest the subjective reviewer flags are too sensitive in these areas; any new findings should be cross-referenced against the 113 and 78 previously resolved issues respectively to avoid re-doing work. Clusters should target concrete code changes, not reviewer opinion alignment.\",\n  \"organize_guidance\": \"Priority order: (1) Duplication boilerplate issues - 6/6 failing with 0.3 pass rate is the most actionable detector-level failure. (2) Error consistency - address the one open finding plus any new ones from scanning, but avoid the re-flagging trap by checking against resolved IDs. (3) Low elegance - the two open findings (lifecycle_create_inline_orchestration, normalizer_main_loop_phase_density) are concrete and actionable. (4) Mid elegance - the open pr_merge_handler_wide_boundary finding. (5) File health structural issues (6 failing). Avoid creating clusters for Abstraction fit, Convention drift, or any dimension above 93. Do not re-cluster previously resolved areas without evidence of new code changes in those files.\",\n  \"sense_check_guidance\": \"Watch for three value traps: (1) Abstraction fit rework - the reviewer will keep flagging single-impl interfaces and passthrough delegation as problems; these are intentional DI patterns and fixing them would violate project architecture principles. Skip or false-positive these. (2) Test health score inflation - the 28.6-point gap between strict (87.2) and verified (58.6) means test coverage claims are not trustworthy. Any cluster claiming to fix test health should demonstrate actual coverage improvement, not just detector satisfaction. (3) Error consistency churn - with 113 resolved and 8 reopened, the dimension has the worst resolve-to-reopen ratio. New error consistency work should target the specific open finding (no_error_cause_chaining) rather than broad sweeps that get re-flagged.\",\n  \"anti_patterns\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"rework-loop\",\n      \"description\": \"Error consistency has 113 resolved issues but 8 reopens, and the dimension score DECLINED from 88.5 to 86.0 despite all that work. This is the clearest rework loop in the history.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"error_consistency: 113 resolved, 8 reopened, score went from 88.5 to 86.0 (declining trend)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"dimension-neglect\",\n      \"description\": \"Low elegance (w=12) has zero recent investment and is stagnant at 87.5 with 12.5 headroom. This high-weight dimension is being ignored in favor of lower-weight ones.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Low elegance: recent_investment=0, headroom=12.5, weight=12, trend=stagnant\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"score-neutral-churn\",\n      \"description\": \"Abstraction fit has 83 resolved issues and 6 reopens but score only moved from 88.5 to 89.5 - a 1-point gain for massive effort. The reviewer keeps re-flagging SOLID patterns.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"abstraction_fitness: 83 resolved, 6 reopened, net score delta = +1.0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"skip-heavy-execution\",\n      \"description\": \"46.4% skip rate (199 skipped of 429 total). While 145 are false-positives (healthy), 20 temporary skips and 34 unaccounted suggest some avoidance.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"execution_patterns: skip_rate=0.464, total_skipped=199, false_positive=145, temporary=20\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"growing-wontfix-debt\",\n      \"description\": \"205 current wontfix issues represent accepted technical debt that weighs on strict scores, particularly Duplication (12.7 gap between score and strict).\",\n      \"evidence\": \"debt_trajectory: current_wontfix=205, worst_dimension=Duplication, worst_dimension_gap=12.7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"score-plateau\",\n      \"description\": \"Three consecutive scans at 90.6 indicate the current approach has exhausted easy gains. Breaking through requires targeting the highest-headroom, highest-weight dimensions.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"strict_scores: [88.8, 88.5, 90.6, 90.6, 90.6]\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"strategic_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"error-consistency-regression\",\n      \"summary\": \"Error consistency is the only high-weight dimension actively declining despite heavy prior investment\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Focus narrowly on the one open finding (no_error_cause_chaining) and avoid broad error consistency sweeps. The 113-resolved-8-reopened pattern suggests the reviewer is too aggressive; use false-positive skips for any re-flagged patterns that match previously resolved IDs.\",\n      \"dimensions_affected\": [\"Error consistency\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"test-health-verified-gap\",\n      \"summary\": \"Test health verified_strict_score (58.6) is 28.6 points below strict score (87.2), indicating unreliable coverage metrics\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Investigate why verified_strict_score diverges so dramatically from strict. The 7 failing checks may be masking deeper coverage gaps. Do not trust test_coverage detector results at face value until this gap is understood.\",\n      \"dimensions_affected\": [\"Test health\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"duplication-boilerplate-outlier\",\n      \"summary\": \"Boilerplate duplication detector has 0.3 pass rate (6/6 failing) - worst single-detector pass rate in the entire scorecard\",\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Target boilerplate duplication as the highest-ROI detector fix. The files involved (authenticated-git-ops.ts, repo-detector.ts, lifecycle-report.ts, labels/processor.ts, repo-settings/processor.ts, repo/utils.ts) are known and concrete.\",\n      \"dimensions_affected\": [\"Duplication\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"low-elegance-neglect\",\n      \"summary\": \"Low elegance (w=12) has zero investment across all tracked cycles despite 12.5 headroom and stagnant trend\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Create a cluster targeting the two open findings: lifecycle_create_inline_orchestration and normalizer_main_loop_phase_density. These are concrete refactoring targets with measurable impact on a high-weight dimension.\",\n      \"dimensions_affected\": [\"Low elegance\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"abstraction-fit-churn-trap\",\n      \"summary\": \"Abstraction fit has consumed massive effort (83 resolved) for only 1 point of score improvement due to SOLID false positives\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Suppress recurring abstraction_fitness findings that flag single-impl interfaces, passthrough delegation, and options bags. These are intentional architectural patterns per CLAUDE.md. Do not create new clusters targeting this dimension.\",\n      \"dimensions_affected\": [\"Abstraction fit\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
