        "observe": {
          "stage": "observe",
          "report": "OBSERVE STAGE REPORT - Verified all 13 open review issues against actual source code.\n\n## Per-Issue Assessments\n\n- hash: 388c002b\n  id: review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::repo_iteration_context_mixed_concerns\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: RepoIterationContext (repo-sync-runner.ts lines 31-44) has 12 fields mixing immutable deps (config, options, branchName, processor, lifecycleManager, tokenManager, factories, logger, executor) with mutable accumulators (reportResults, lifecycleReportInputs, settingsCollector). The issue is technically real. However, splitting into RepoSyncDeps + RepoSyncCollectors adds 2 types to replace 1, and every callsite would need both. The struct is only created once (sync-command.ts line 142) and consumed in one place (runSingleRepo). The mutation contract is already clear from the types: arrays and ResultsCollector are obviously mutable. Splitting gains type-level immutability signaling but adds indirection for a single-consumer context bag.\n  files_read: [src/cli/repo-sync-runner.ts, src/cli/sync-command.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip -- single-consumer context bag, splitting adds type surface without proportional clarity gain\n\n- hash: b583cf08\n  id: review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::code_scanning_inline_params_type\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: ICodeScanningStrategy.update (code-scanning/types.ts lines 23-27) takes an inline anonymous type { state: string; query_suite?: string; languages?: string[] }. Sibling strategies use named param types: ILabelsStrategy uses LabelUpdateParams (labels/types.ts line 22), IRulesetStrategy uses RulesetUpdateParams (rulesets/types.ts line 43). The inconsistency is real and the inline type makes it harder to share or extend the params. Extracting a named CodeScanningUpdateParams is trivial and aligns with established convention.\n  files_read: [src/settings/code-scanning/types.ts, src/settings/labels/types.ts, src/settings/rulesets/types.ts]\n  recommendation: Fix -- extract named CodeScanningUpdateParams type, trivial change matching sibling convention\n\n- hash: 09447f39\n  id: review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::github_pr_strategy_module_level_helpers\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: getRepoFlag (line 28) and buildPRUrlRegex (line 35) are module-level functions in github-pr-strategy.ts. GitLabPRStrategy uses private methods (getRepoFlag at line 38, buildMRUrl at line 45). AdoPRStrategy also uses private methods (getOrgUrl at line 33, buildPRUrl at line 37). The inconsistency is real. However, getRepoFlag is also called from the merge() method at line 264 to log a message -- having it as a module function is actually slightly cleaner since it is a pure function that does not need this context. Moving these inside the class is a cosmetic alignment that adds unnecessary this context to pure functions. Module-level pure functions are arguably better than private methods for stateless helpers.\n  files_read: [src/vcs/github-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/ado-pr-strategy.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip -- module-level pure functions are preferable for stateless helpers, cosmetic alignment not worth the churn\n\n- hash: 135b11e0\n  id: review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::dead_re_export_formatDiffLine\n  verdict: false-positive\n  verdict_reasoning: The issue claims output/index.ts re-exports formatDiffLine from shared/diff-format.js. Verified output/index.ts (lines 1-31) -- formatDiffLine is NOT re-exported anywhere in that file. The only consumers of formatDiffLine are sync/diff-utils.ts (line 3, imports from ../shared/diff-format.js) and output/sync-report.ts (line 4, imports from ../shared/diff-format.js). Both import directly from shared/, not via output/index.ts. This issue describes code that no longer exists -- resolved during commit d7f9423 which moved diff-format to shared/.\n  files_read: [src/output/index.ts, src/shared/diff-format.ts, src/sync/diff-utils.ts, src/output/sync-report.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip -- the dead re-export no longer exists\n\n- hash: ced10f5d\n  id: review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::self_referencing_import_path\n  verdict: false-positive\n  verdict_reasoning: The issue claims shared/interpolation-engine.ts uses '../shared/type-guards.js' instead of './type-guards.js'. Verified at line 11 of interpolation-engine.ts: the import is \"import { isPlainObject } from './type-guards.js'\" -- a correct relative import within the same directory. No '../shared/' self-referencing import exists. This was resolved during commit d7f9423 which moved interpolation-engine.ts into shared/.\n  files_read: [src/shared/interpolation-engine.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip -- already using correct './type-guards.js' import path\n\n- hash: 1525e7e1\n  id: review::.::holistic::dependency_health::pretry_version_mismatch\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: package.json line 77 specifies \"p-retry\": \"^8.0.0\" but node_modules/p-retry/package.json shows version 7.1.1 installed. This is a real version mismatch -- npm should have installed 8.x per the spec but the lockfile pins 7.1.1. The codebase is tested against 7.x but declares 8.x compatibility. Either the lockfile needs regenerating or the package.json spec needs downgrading to ^7.1.1.\n  files_read: [package.json, node_modules/p-retry/package.json]\n  recommendation: Fix -- align package.json spec with installed version, either update lockfile to get 8.x or downgrade spec to ^7.1.1\n\n- hash: a266478e\n  id: review::.::holistic::error_consistency::no_error_cause_chaining\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Verified ~21 catch-and-rethrow sites across the codebase (loader.ts has 6, file-reference-resolver.ts has 2, manifest.ts has 1, lifecycle modules have several, PR strategies have 3, group-validator has 1). None of them pass { cause: error } as the second argument. Examples: loader.ts line 23 throws new ValidationError with toErrorMessage(error) but no cause; ado-migration-source.ts line 47 same pattern. The custom errors (ValidationError, SyncError, LifecycleError) all extend Error which accepts ErrorOptions with cause. All stack traces are lost on rethrow, replaced only by the message text. This is a genuine and systemic pattern issue across ~21 sites with zero usage of cause chaining.\n  files_read: [src/config/loader.ts, src/config/file-reference-resolver.ts, src/sync/manifest.ts, src/lifecycle/ado-migration-source.ts, src/vcs/ado-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts]\n  recommendation: Fix -- add { cause: error } to all catch-and-rethrow sites. Medium effort (~21 sites) but mechanical and safe.\n\n- hash: 5ca95c69\n  id: review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::inconsistent_switch_exhaustiveness\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Several switch statements on union types use inconsistent exhaustiveness patterns. lifecycle-report.ts line 71 and formatter.ts line 53 use the _exhaustive:never pattern correctly. PR strategies (github-pr-strategy.ts line 312, ado-pr-strategy.ts line 289, gitlab-pr-strategy.ts line 328) use const _exhaustive: \"direct\" = config.mode which is typed but does not use never. labels/processor.ts line 92 switches on action (\"create\"|\"update\"|\"delete\"|\"unchanged\") with cases for create/update/delete but no unchanged or default case. rulesets/processor.ts line 109 has all 4 cases but neither processor uses a never-exhaustive check. unified-summary.ts line 152 has a switch with 3 of 4 lifecycle actions and no default. The inconsistency is real across at least 5 files.\n  files_read: [src/output/lifecycle-report.ts, src/lifecycle/formatter.ts, src/vcs/github-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/ado-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts, src/settings/labels/processor.ts, src/settings/rulesets/processor.ts, src/cli/unified-summary.ts, src/vcs/pr-strategy-factory.ts]\n  recommendation: Fix -- add exhaustiveness checks to switch statements on union types that lack them. Small effort, prevents silent bugs when union types are extended.\n\n- hash: 4a2c008c\n  id: review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::pr_creator_catch_all_default\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: pr-creator.ts formatFileChanges (lines 80-93) has a switch on f.action (type \"create\"|\"update\"|\"skip\"|\"delete\") with cases for create, update, delete, and a catch-all default: actionText = \"Changed\". The skip case is filtered out by line 78 (files.filter(f => f.action !== \"skip\")), so skip should never reach the switch. But the default masks any future FileActionKind additions at compile time. Replacing default with explicit handling and a never-exhaustive check would catch new action types at compile time.\n  files_read: [src/vcs/pr-creator.ts, src/vcs/types.ts]\n  recommendation: Fix -- replace default with explicit skip case and add never-exhaustive check. Trivial change.\n\n- hash: 550aefbe\n  id: review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lifecycle_create_inline_orchestration\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: GitHubLifecycleProvider.create() (lines 230-297, 67 lines) chains: create repo, detect actual branch, rename if different, wait for propagation, delete readme. The post-creation steps are already well-structured -- renameBranch (line 280), waitForDefaultBranch (line 289), and deleteReadme (line 296) are all extracted as private methods. The only inline logic is the branch detection (lines 264-277, ~13 lines) which fetches the actual default branch and compares it. Extracting an ensureDefaultBranch helper would wrap 15 lines of already-clean code into yet another private method for marginal readability gain. The create() method reads clearly top-to-bottom with inline comments.\n  files_read: [src/lifecycle/github-lifecycle-provider.ts]\n  recommendation: Skip -- the method is 67 lines with heavy work already extracted into private methods. Further extraction adds indirection for minimal gain.\n\n- hash: a67f6445\n  id: review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::normalizer_main_loop_phase_density\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: normalizeConfig (normalizer.ts lines 642-764, 122 lines) has a main loop body (lines 648-748, ~100 lines) packing 4 phases: expand extends (2 lines), merge groups (6 lines), merge conditional groups (14 lines), then per-git-URL file/settings/PR resolution (~65 lines). The inner per-git-URL loop (lines 697-747) does file resolution, repo-only file processing, PR option merging, settings merging, and assembling RepoConfig. This is the densest function in the normalizer and the per-repo processing would benefit from extraction into normalizeRepoEntry() to match the extraction style already used by mergeGroupFiles/mergeGroupSettings helper functions.\n  files_read: [src/config/normalizer.ts]\n  recommendation: Fix -- extract per-repo processing into normalizeRepoEntry(). Medium effort but improves readability of a critical function.\n\n- hash: 2d20e3dc\n  id: review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::pr_merge_handler_wide_boundary\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: CreateAndMergeInput (sync/types.ts lines 239-247) takes full repoConfig: RepoConfig, which includes files (FileContent[]), settings (RepoSettings), upstream, source -- none of which PRMergeHandler uses. In pr-merge-handler.ts, the handler accesses only repoConfig.prOptions (lines 43, 48, 56, 57, 58) for merge mode, strategy, deleteBranch, bypassReason, and labels. The other RepoConfig fields (files, settings, upstream, source) cross the boundary unnecessarily. Narrowing CreateAndMergeInput to carry only prOptions and labels would make the dependency explicit and prevent the handler from ever reaching into unrelated config sections.\n  files_read: [src/sync/types.ts, src/sync/pr-merge-handler.ts]\n  recommendation: Fix -- narrow CreateAndMergeInput to replace repoConfig with the specific prOptions fields used. Small effort, improves boundary clarity.\n\n- hash: 77029939\n  id: review::.::holistic::type_safety::code_scanning_validation_unlinked_types\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: In config/validators/shared.ts lines 163-175, VALID_CODE_SCANNING_STATES, VALID_CODE_SCANNING_QUERY_SUITES, and VALID_CODE_SCANNING_LANGUAGES are plain string arrays not linked to the type aliases CodeScanningState, CodeScanningQuerySuite, CodeScanningLanguage defined in config/types.ts (lines 369-385). Meanwhile, sibling validators already use validValues<T>(): repo-settings-validator.ts uses validValues<RepoVisibility> (line 16), file-validator.ts uses validValues<ArrayMergeStrategy> (line 15), ruleset-validator.ts has 8 instances (lines 21-58). The pattern exists and is established -- shared.ts is the only validator not using it for code scanning types.\n  files_read: [src/config/validators/shared.ts, src/config/types.ts, src/config/validators/repo-settings-validator.ts, src/config/validators/file-validator.ts, src/config/validators/ruleset-validator.ts]\n  recommendation: Fix -- apply validValues<T>() pattern to the 3 code scanning arrays. Trivial change using established pattern.\n\n## Auto-Cluster Sampling\n\nNo named auto-clusters are defined. The 207 unclustered items span exports, smells, structural, boilerplate_duplication, props, unused, and test_coverage detectors. Sampled representative items:\n\n- cluster: unclustered/exports-dead-code\n  verdict: mixed\n  sample_count: 5\n  false_positive_rate: 0.40\n  recommendation: break_up\n  reasoning: Sampled 5 dead export items from src/config/index.ts barrel (PullRequestRuleParameters, RULESET_COMPARABLE_FIELDS, RawConfig, RawFileConfig, RawRepoConfig). RawConfig is consumed externally by CLI and tests. RULESET_COMPARABLE_FIELDS is used in rulesets/diff.ts. PullRequestRuleParameters may be genuinely dead. The barrel re-export pattern causes the detector to miss transitive usage. Need individual verification rather than bulk action.\n\n- cluster: unclustered/remaining-backlog\n  verdict: mixed\n  sample_count: 0\n  false_positive_rate: N/A\n  recommendation: defer\n  reasoning: The remaining ~197 items need deferred investigation. Per strategize guidance, boilerplate_duplication items (6/6 failing with 0.3 pass rate) are the highest-value subset and should be assessed individually in a future cycle.\n\n## Summary\n- 2 false positives: [135b11e0] dead_re_export_formatDiffLine (already removed), [ced10f5d] self_referencing_import_path (already fixed)\n- 8 genuine actionable: [b583cf08] code_scanning_inline_params_type, [1525e7e1] pretry_version_mismatch, [a266478e] no_error_cause_chaining, [5ca95c69] inconsistent_switch_exhaustiveness, [4a2c008c] pr_creator_catch_all_default, [a67f6445] normalizer_main_loop_phase_density, [2d20e3dc] pr_merge_handler_wide_boundary, [77029939] code_scanning_validation_unlinked_types\n- 3 not-worth-it: [388c002b] repo_iteration_context_mixed_concerns (single-consumer bag), [09447f39] github_pr_strategy_module_level_helpers (pure functions better as module-level), [550aefbe] lifecycle_create_inline_orchestration (already well-extracted)",
