        "reflect": {
          "stage": "reflect",
          "report": "## Coverage Ledger\n- code_scanning_inline_params_type -> cluster \"code-scanning-type-alignment\"\n- code_scanning_validation_unlinked_types -> cluster \"code-scanning-type-alignment\"\n- dead_re_export_formatDiffLine -> skip \"false-positive-already-removed\"\n- github_pr_strategy_module_level_helpers -> skip \"not-worth-it-pure-functions-better-as-module-level\"\n- inconsistent_switch_exhaustiveness -> cluster \"switch-exhaustiveness\"\n- lifecycle_create_inline_orchestration -> skip \"not-worth-it-already-well-extracted\"\n- no_error_cause_chaining -> cluster \"error-cause-chaining\"\n- normalizer_main_loop_phase_density -> cluster \"normalizer-density-extraction\"\n- pr_creator_catch_all_default -> cluster \"switch-exhaustiveness\"\n- pr_merge_handler_wide_boundary -> cluster \"pr-merge-boundary-narrowing\"\n- pretry_version_mismatch -> cluster \"pretry-version-fix\"\n- repo_iteration_context_mixed_concerns -> skip \"not-worth-it-single-consumer-context-bag\"\n- self_referencing_import_path -> skip \"false-positive-already-fixed\"\n\n## Cluster Blueprint\n\nCluster \"error-cause-chaining\" (error_consistency dimension, ~21 catch-and-rethrow sites across src/)\n  WHY FIRST: Error consistency is actively declining (88.5 -> 86.0) with 14.0 headroom and is the highest-headroom dimension. This is mechanical work -- add { cause: error } to every catch-and-rethrow. All custom error classes already accept ErrorOptions. Zero risk of behavioral change. High ROI: addresses the sole open error_consistency finding and directly targets the declining dimension.\n  Touches: src/config/loader.ts, src/config/file-reference-resolver.ts, src/sync/manifest.ts, src/lifecycle/ado-migration-source.ts, src/vcs/ado-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts, and ~15 more catch sites.\n  Steps: (1) Grep all catch-and-rethrow patterns. (2) Add { cause: error } as second arg to each throw new XxxError() inside catch blocks. (3) Verify tests still pass.\n  Effort: medium (21 sites, but mechanical find-and-fix)\n  Dependencies: none\n\nCluster \"switch-exhaustiveness\" (logic_clarity dimension, 2 issues touching 5+ files)\n  WHY: Two issues share the exact same fix pattern -- adding `default: { const _exhaustive: never = x; throw new Error(...); }` to switch statements on union types. The established pattern exists in lifecycle-report.ts and formatter.ts. Grouping these lets a single executor apply the same fix pattern across all affected files consistently.\n  Touches: src/vcs/pr-creator.ts, src/vcs/github-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/ado-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts, src/settings/labels/processor.ts, src/settings/rulesets/processor.ts, src/cli/unified-summary.ts\n  Steps: (1) Add never-exhaustive default to each switch on a union type. (2) For pr-creator.ts specifically, replace the catch-all default with explicit skip handling + never check. (3) Type-check to confirm no compile errors.\n  Effort: small (same pattern repeated, trivial per file)\n  Dependencies: none\n\nCluster \"code-scanning-type-alignment\" (api_surface_coherence + type_safety dimensions, 2 issues)\n  WHY: Both issues target code-scanning types and share a root cause: code-scanning module was less carefully typed than its siblings (labels, rulesets). The inline params type in code-scanning/types.ts and the unlinked validation arrays in validators/shared.ts are two facets of the same gap. Fixing together ensures the code-scanning module fully matches sibling conventions in one pass.\n  Touches: src/settings/code-scanning/types.ts, src/config/validators/shared.ts, src/config/types.ts\n  Steps: (1) Extract CodeScanningUpdateParams type in code-scanning/types.ts, update ICodeScanningStrategy.update signature. (2) Apply validValues<T>() to the 3 code-scanning arrays in validators/shared.ts. (3) Type-check.\n  Effort: trivial (both are one-liner type fixes using established patterns)\n  Dependencies: none\n\nCluster \"normalizer-density-extraction\" (low_level_elegance dimension, 1 issue)\n  WHY: Low elegance is stagnant at 87.5 with zero recent investment and 12.5 headroom. This is the only actionable low_level_elegance issue that observe confirmed as genuine. normalizeConfig's 100-line loop body is the densest function in the normalizer, and per-repo processing extraction follows the same pattern already used by mergeGroupFiles/mergeGroupSettings.\n  Touches: src/config/normalizer.ts\n  Steps: (1) Extract per-repo processing (lines 697-747) into normalizeRepoEntry(). (2) Ensure the outer loop calls the extracted function. (3) Run tests to verify behavior preservation.\n  Effort: medium (refactoring a critical path function requires care)\n  Dependencies: none\n\nCluster \"pr-merge-boundary-narrowing\" (mid_level_elegance dimension, 1 issue)\n  WHY: Mid elegance is plateaued at 87.5 with 12.5 headroom on a high-weight dimension (w=22). CreateAndMergeInput passing full RepoConfig when only prOptions is used is a clear ISP violation. Narrowing the boundary improves interface clarity and aligns with the project's SOLID principles.\n  Touches: src/sync/types.ts, src/sync/pr-merge-handler.ts, caller in src/sync/sync-workflow.ts\n  Steps: (1) Define a narrowed type with only prOptions fields. (2) Update CreateAndMergeInput to use it. (3) Update caller in sync-workflow.ts to extract the needed fields. (4) Type-check and test.\n  Effort: small (3 files, straightforward type narrowing)\n  Dependencies: none\n\nCluster \"pretry-version-fix\" (dependency_health dimension, 1 issue)\n  WHY: A version mismatch between declared (^8.0.0) and installed (7.1.1) is a correctness issue that could cause CI failures or unexpected behavior if lockfile regeneration installs 8.x. Quick standalone fix.\n  Touches: package.json (and possibly package-lock.json)\n  Steps: (1) Check if p-retry 8.x has breaking changes. (2) Either update lockfile to get 8.x or downgrade spec to ^7.1.1. (3) Run tests to verify compatibility.\n  Effort: trivial\n  Dependencies: none (but should be done first since it's a dependency issue)\n\n## Execution Order\n\n1. pretry-version-fix (trivial, standalone dependency fix, do first to avoid lockfile conflicts)\n2. error-cause-chaining (highest-headroom declining dimension, mechanical, no conflicts)\n3. switch-exhaustiveness (small effort, multiple files but same pattern)\n4. code-scanning-type-alignment (trivial, isolated to code-scanning module)\n5. pr-merge-boundary-narrowing (small, touches sync/ types)\n6. normalizer-density-extraction (medium effort, refactoring critical path -- do last to avoid conflicts)\n\n## Backlog Decisions\n- unclustered/exports-dead-code -> defer \"40% false positive rate per observe sampling means each item needs individual verification; barrel re-exports cause false detections. Not worth bulk action this cycle. Revisit after higher-impact clusters complete.\"\n- unclustered/remaining-backlog -> defer \"197 items need individual assessment. Per strategize, boilerplate_duplication (6/6 failing, 0.3 pass rate) is the highest-value subset but requires dedicated investigation cycle. Deferring all remaining backlog to next triage cycle.\"\n\n## Skip Decisions\nSkip \"false-positive-already-removed\": dead_re_export_formatDiffLine -- observe confirmed the re-export was removed in commit d7f9423. No code exists to fix.\nSkip \"false-positive-already-fixed\": self_referencing_import_path -- observe confirmed the import already uses correct './type-guards.js' path since commit d7f9423.\nSkip \"not-worth-it-single-consumer-context-bag\": repo_iteration_context_mixed_concerns -- single-consumer context bag created in one place (sync-command.ts line 142) and consumed in one place (runSingleRepo). Splitting into two types adds type surface without proportional clarity gain. The mutation contract is already clear from array/collector types.\nSkip \"not-worth-it-pure-functions-better-as-module-level\": github_pr_strategy_module_level_helpers -- getRepoFlag and buildPRUrlRegex are stateless pure functions. Module-level pure functions are arguably preferable to private methods that unnecessarily bind stateless logic to a class instance. Cosmetic alignment with siblings not worth the churn.\nSkip \"not-worth-it-already-well-extracted\": lifecycle_create_inline_orchestration -- create() is 67 lines with renameBranch, waitForDefaultBranch, and deleteReadme already extracted as private methods. The remaining inline logic is 13 lines of branch detection. Further extraction wraps already-clean code in yet another method for negligible readability gain.\n\n## Recurring Pattern Analysis\n- error_consistency: 113 resolved, 8 reopened, score declining. The rework loop is driven by the subjective reviewer being too aggressive. This cycle has exactly ONE genuine finding (no_error_cause_chaining) which is a concrete, mechanical fix across 21 sites. This is NOT a subjective reviewer opinion issue -- it is a missing language feature usage. The cluster targets the specific fix, not broad error pattern alignment, which should break the reopen cycle.\n- low_level_elegance: 68 resolved, 2 new open. Observe confirmed 1 genuine (normalizer density) and 1 not-worth-it (lifecycle create). The dimension has had zero recent investment despite w=12 and 12.5 headroom. The normalizer extraction is the right investment -- a concrete refactoring of the densest function in a critical module.\n- mid_level_elegance: 78 resolved, 1 new open. The pr_merge_handler_wide_boundary finding is genuine ISP improvement on a high-weight dimension (w=22). Unlike prior mid-elegance work that got re-flagged, this is a type-level change with clear before/after, making reopen unlikely.\n- logic_clarity: The 2 switch exhaustiveness findings are related to each other but unrelated to the previously resolved redundant_changed_param_file_writer. This is a new pattern (missing never-exhaustive checks) not a recurrence of prior work.",
