          "report": "SENSE-CHECK REPORT\n\n## Content Check\n\n### 1. pretry-version-fix\n- STALENESS: NOT stale. The enrich report incorrectly stated \"no actual mismatch found.\" npm ls p-retry shows p-retry@7.1.1 installed but package.json specifies ^8.0.0. This IS a real version mismatch.\n- LINE NUMBERS: package.json line 77 has \"p-retry\": \"^8.0.0\". Correct.\n- NAMES: src/shared/retry-utils.ts imports from \"p-retry\". Correct.\n- EFFORT: trivial is correct \u2014 it's a one-line version spec change.\n- TIGHTEN NEEDED: Step description says \"verify by running npm ls\" but should say \"fix the spec to match installed version (^7.0.0) or run npm install to upgrade.\" The step says the spec and lockfile are already aligned, which is WRONG. Updated step detail to correct this.\n\n### 2. error-cause-chaining\n- STALENESS: NOT stale. Verified zero { cause: } usage across all 10 target files.\n- COUNTS: 21 catch-and-rethrow sites verified across 10 files: loader.ts (6), git-ops.ts (6), file-reference-resolver.ts (2), manifest.ts (1), group-validator.ts (1), ado-pr-strategy.ts (1), gitlab-pr-strategy.ts (1), github-pr-strategy.ts (1), ado-migration-source.ts (1), json-utils.ts (1). Count is CORRECT.\n- LINE NUMBERS: All verified against current source. loader.ts catch blocks at lines 22, 47, 57, 76, 101, 111. git-ops.ts at lines 65, 83, 102, 123, 147, 306. file-reference-resolver.ts at lines 65, 103. manifest.ts at line 210. group-validator.ts at line 85. ado-pr-strategy.ts at line 170. gitlab-pr-strategy.ts at line 212. github-pr-strategy.ts at line 143. ado-migration-source.ts at line 45. json-utils.ts at line 12.\n- OVER-ENGINEERING: No. Adding { cause: error } is a pure improvement \u2014 preserves error chain context for debugging at zero complexity cost.\n- EFFORT: medium is correct \u2014 21 sites across 10 files, mechanical but needs care.\n\n### 3. switch-exhaustiveness\n- STALENESS: NOT stale. All 4 switches verified as lacking exhaustive defaults.\n- NAMES/LINE NUMBERS verified:\n  - src/vcs/pr-creator.ts line 81: switch on f.action (FileActionKind) with catch-all default at line 91. CONFIRMED.\n  - src/cli/unified-summary.ts line 152: switch on lcAction.action (LifecycleActionKind) with no default. \"existed\" is filtered by if-guard at line 150, remaining cases are \"created\"/\"forked\"/\"migrated\" \u2014 all covered but no never-exhaustive default. CONFIRMED.\n  - src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts line 82: getMergeStrategyFlag switch on MergeStrategy with catch-all default at line 88. CONFIRMED.\n  - src/vcs/github-pr-strategy.ts line 222: getMergeStrategyFlag switch on MergeStrategy with catch-all default at line 229. CONFIRMED.\n- OVER-ENGINEERING: No. never-exhaustive defaults are a standard TypeScript safety pattern.\n- EFFORT: step 1 small, step 2 trivial. Correct.\n- NOTE: The step says to replace pr-creator.ts default with explicit 'skip' case \u2014 this is slightly wrong. Since 'skip' is filtered out at line 77, the correct approach is to handle 'skip' unreachable + add never-exhaustive default. But the overall direction is correct and an executor would understand.\n\n### 4. code-scanning-type-alignment\n- STALENESS: NOT stale. src/settings/code-scanning/types.ts line 23-26 shows inline params type `{ state: string; query_suite?: string; languages?: string[] }` on ICodeScanningStrategy.update. src/config/validators/shared.ts lines 163-175 show plain string arrays without type linkage to CodeScanningState types.\n- NAMES: validValues<T> pattern confirmed at src/config/validators/ruleset-validator.ts:15 and src/config/validators/file-validator.ts:9. VALID_CODE_SCANNING_STATES, VALID_CODE_SCANNING_QUERY_SUITES, VALID_CODE_SCANNING_LANGUAGES confirmed at shared.ts lines 163-175.\n- OVER-ENGINEERING: No. Named type extraction for a 3-field inline type is standard. validValues<T> is an existing pattern already used in the codebase.\n- EFFORT: trivial + trivial. Correct.\n- NOTE: Step 1 says \"Import the validValues<T> helper from ruleset-validator.ts (or duplicate the 3-line function locally).\" The function is ALREADY duplicated in file-validator.ts, so duplicating locally is the established pattern. This is a reasonable choice. Should be tightened to recommend duplication (not import) to match codebase convention.\n\n### 5. pr-merge-boundary-narrowing\n- STALENESS: NOT stale. CreateAndMergeInput at src/sync/types.ts line 239 carries full RepoConfig. PRMergeHandler at src/sync/pr-merge-handler.ts accesses ONLY repoConfig.prOptions (5 fields: labels line 43, merge line 48, mergeStrategy line 56, deleteBranch line 57, bypassReason line 58). CONFIRMED.\n- LINE NUMBERS: All correct.\n- NAMES: CreateAndMergeInput, PRMergeHandler, RepoConfig all exist. PRMergeOptions does not yet exist \u2014 it would be a new type. This is correctly described as something to create.\n- OVER-ENGINEERING: No. This is a pure ISP narrowing that removes unnecessary coupling. The PRMergeHandler currently receives the entire RepoConfig but only needs prOptions. The change is straightforward and reduces surface area.\n- EFFORT: small. Correct \u2014 touches 3 files (types.ts, pr-merge-handler.ts, sync-workflow.ts).\n\n### 6. normalizer-density-extraction\n- STALENESS: NOT stale. normalizeConfig main loop at src/config/normalizer.ts lines 697-747 is a 50-line loop body.\n- LINE NUMBERS: Verified. The per-gitUrl loop body runs from line 697 to 747.\n- COUNTS: The step says 9 parameters. Verified: gitUrl, effectiveRootFiles, rawRepo, fileNames, repoOnlyFileNames, effectivePROptions, effectiveSettings, raw.deleteOrphaned, env. That's 9. CORRECT.\n- OVER-ENGINEERING CONCERN: This extraction creates a single-consumer function with 9 parameters. The current loop body is already locally readable within normalizeConfig. Extracting it would:\n  - ADD a 9-parameter function signature (net line increase)\n  - Create a function called from exactly ONE place\n  - Not improve testability (private function, same file)\n  However, the loop body IS dense and mixing multiple phases (resolve files, resolve repo-only files, merge prOptions, merge settings, push result). The extraction would clarify the per-repo boundary. On balance, this is borderline but acceptable given the high-weight dimension (low_level_elegance, w=12).\n- EFFORT: medium. Correct.\n\n## Structure Check\n\n### File-touch graph\n- pretry-version-fix: package.json, src/shared/retry-utils.ts\n- error-cause-chaining: src/config/loader.ts, src/vcs/git-ops.ts, src/config/file-reference-resolver.ts, src/sync/manifest.ts, src/config/validators/group-validator.ts, src/vcs/ado-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/github-pr-strategy.ts, src/lifecycle/ado-migration-source.ts, src/shared/json-utils.ts\n- switch-exhaustiveness: src/vcs/pr-creator.ts, src/cli/unified-summary.ts, src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts, src/vcs/github-pr-strategy.ts\n- code-scanning-type-alignment: src/config/validators/shared.ts, src/settings/code-scanning/types.ts, src/settings/code-scanning/github-code-scanning-strategy.ts\n- pr-merge-boundary-narrowing: src/sync/types.ts, src/sync/pr-merge-handler.ts, src/sync/sync-workflow.ts\n- normalizer-density-extraction: src/config/normalizer.ts\n\n### Shared files\n- src/vcs/gitlab-pr-strategy.ts: touched by BOTH error-cause-chaining AND switch-exhaustiveness\n- src/vcs/github-pr-strategy.ts: touched by BOTH error-cause-chaining AND switch-exhaustiveness\n\nBoth overlaps are low-risk \u2014 error-cause-chaining modifies catch blocks while switch-exhaustiveness modifies switch statements (different code regions). However, since they touch the same files, a --depends-on is warranted.\n\nACTION: switch-exhaustiveness should depend on error-cause-chaining (run error-cause first, since it touches more of these files).\n\n### Missing cascades: None detected. All clusters are self-contained.\n### Circular dependencies: None detected.\n\n## Value Check (YAGNI/KISS)\n\n### pretry-version-fix\nThe mismatch is real (^8.0.0 spec vs 7.1.1 installed). This is a dependency health issue that could cause confusion or breakage on fresh install. Fixing it is trivial and valuable.\nDecision: **tighten** \u2014 step detail incorrectly says \"no mismatch found.\" Must correct to acknowledge the real mismatch and specify whether to downgrade spec to ^7.0.0 or upgrade the installed version to 8.x.\n\n### error-cause-chaining\nAdding { cause: error } to all catch-and-rethrow sites is a well-established Node.js best practice (available since Node 16). It preserves error chain context for debugging with zero overhead. 21 sites is mechanical work but high value for error diagnostics.\nDecision: **keep**\n\n### switch-exhaustiveness\nNever-exhaustive defaults are a standard TypeScript compile-time safety pattern. All 4 switches operate on union types where new members would silently fall through. This is a correctness improvement.\nDecision: **keep**\n\n### code-scanning-type-alignment\nExtracting a named type from an inline params object and applying the existing validValues<T> pattern improves type safety and consistency with sibling validators. Both changes are small, concrete, and follow established codebase patterns.\nDecision: **keep**\n\n### pr-merge-boundary-narrowing\nPure ISP narrowing: PRMergeHandler receives full RepoConfig but only uses prOptions (5 fields). Narrowing to carry just prOptions reduces coupling and makes the dependency explicit. Clean, focused change touching 3 files.\nDecision: **keep**\n\n### normalizer-density-extraction\nExtracting a 50-line loop body into a 9-parameter helper function is borderline. The loop body is dense but readable in context. The extraction would create a single-consumer function that increases net line count. However, the normalizeConfig function is already large and the per-repo boundary is a natural extraction point. The high-weight dimension (low_level_elegance w=12, 12.5 headroom) justifies the investment.\nDecision: **tighten** \u2014 step should specify that the function should use an options object (not 9 positional parameters) to keep the extraction clean. A 9-positional-parameter function is itself a code smell.\n\n## Decision Ledger\n- pretry-version-fix -> tighten (step detail incorrectly says no mismatch; must correct to fix real ^8.0.0 vs 7.1.1 gap)\n- error-cause-chaining -> keep (21 sites verified, zero existing cause chaining, mechanical but high-value)\n- switch-exhaustiveness -> keep (4 switches verified, standard TypeScript safety pattern)\n- code-scanning-type-alignment -> keep (follows existing validValues<T> pattern, named type extraction)\n- pr-merge-boundary-narrowing -> keep (pure ISP narrowing, 5 prOptions fields only, 3 files)\n- normalizer-density-extraction -> tighten (use options object instead of 9 positional params)",
