      "executive_summary": "The codebase has reached 90.6 strict score (all-time high) with an improving trend, but momentum is stalling. Three consecutive scans at 90.6 suggest the easy gains are exhausted. The highest-leverage opportunities are now in neglected high-weight dimensions: Low elegance (w=12, stagnant at 87.5), Mid elegance (w=22, plateaued at 87.5), and Error consistency (w=3, actively declining to 86.0). Duplication is the worst strict dimension at 85.9 with a 0.3 pass rate on boilerplate_duplication, making it a clear target.\n\nThe execution pattern reveals a 46.4% skip rate (199 skipped vs 132 done) with 145 false-positive skips. This is healthy triaging, not avoidance - but the 205 wontfix count is concerning. The rework loops in error_consistency (8 reopens), mid_level_elegance (10 reopens), and abstraction_fitness (6 reopens) indicate the subjective reviewer keeps re-flagging resolved patterns. For abstraction_fitness specifically, this is driven by the reviewer not understanding SOLID DI patterns, and further investment there should be avoided.\n\nTest health shows the most alarming discrepancy: strict score 87.2 vs verified_strict_score 58.6. This 28.6-point gap suggests the test coverage detector is being overly generous, or coverage claims are not matching reality. This dimension also declined from 94.5 to 87.2 and has been flat for 4 scans. Addressing test health would have outsized impact on real codebase resilience even if it does not move the headline score much.",
